*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- drilling rotations
* FIXROT fixes the rotation about Z of the mat nodes that carry shells only.  At the twelve column
* bases the torsion of the column and of the braces would be the only stiffness about Z (local
* modes of these nodes at 7-13 Hz): the base plate is anchored, so D fixes ROTZ there too.  This does not hold the mat's torsion, which the
* soil resists through the translations of the interaction nodes (a flat SHELL has no stiffness about
* its normal).  The floor nodes get their stiffness about Z from the beams (weak-axis bending).
FIXROT
D,17,29,4,1,ROTZ
D,77,89,4,1,ROTZ
D,137,149,4,1,ROTZ
